{
  "title": "Chain rule through a loss",
  "function": "squared_error_grad_w",
  "params": [
    {
      "name": "x",
      "type": "float"
    },
    {
      "name": "w",
      "type": "float"
    },
    {
      "name": "b",
      "type": "float"
    },
    {
      "name": "target",
      "type": "float"
    }
  ],
  "returns": "float",
  "library": true,
  "hints": [
    "There are three links in this chain: L = (y − t)², y = σ(z), z = w·x + b.",
    "∂L/∂y = 2(y − t), ∂y/∂z = σ'(z), ∂z/∂w = x. Multiply them together.",
    "z = w*x + b; y = sigmoid(z); return 2*(y − target) * sigmoid_derivative(z) * x"
  ],
  "tests": [
    {
      "args": [
        1,
        0,
        0,
        1
      ],
      "description": "prediction 0.5, target 1: increase w",
      "expected": -0.25
    },
    {
      "args": [
        2,
        0.5,
        -1,
        0
      ],
      "description": "prediction 0.5, target 0: decrease w",
      "expected": 0.5
    },
    {
      "args": [
        1.5,
        -0.4,
        0.2,
        0.3
      ],
      "description": "a general case",
      "hidden": true,
      "expected": 0.07302413500260466
    },
    {
      "args": [
        0,
        2,
        0,
        0.5
      ],
      "description": "prediction equals target, so the gradient is 0",
      "hidden": true,
      "expected": 0.0
    },
    {
      "args": [
        -2,
        1,
        1,
        1
      ],
      "description": "a negative input",
      "hidden": true,
      "expected": 0.5749393618288605
    }
  ]
}
